**Key findings:**
- **Study ID:** Ge2024
- **Title:** Normative modelling of brain morphometry across the lifespan with CentileBrain: algorithm benchmarking and model optimisation
- **Journal:** The Lancet Digital Health, 2024
- **DOI:** 10.1016/S2589-7500(23)00250-X
- **Sample Size:** 37,407 healthy individuals from 87 datasets.
- **Method:** Benchmarked 8 algorithms, establishing MFPR (Multivariate Fractional Polynomial Regression) as the optimal approach.
- **Validation:** Internal (5-fold CV) and External (longitudinal and clinical cohorts).
- **Clinical Application:** Applied to the HCP-EP cohort (early psychosis) to demonstrate utility in diagnostic classification.

